# assist/procedure.aip
#
# The orchestrator: a task in, the catalog's procedures run one after another until the task is
# done, a procedure built when none fits, and the person asked when it is stuck. It is the
# harness of examples/harness/assist.py written as a procedure, so the top loop is recorded and
# audited like every run beneath it, and `aip runah assist -i '{"task": "...", "outcome": ""}'`
# needs no Python of its own.
#
# One model call per pass (`plan`, which has no aip verbs) and one script (`act`), which holds
# the only verbs there are: run a procedure, carry on a run it started, and, when
# build_procedure has built one, publish it under its new name. It never retires, pins or
# publishes over a name, and it refuses to run assist. Each run it starts is a child of this one
# (`parent` on its record), one level deeper (`aip config runah --max-depth`), and spends from
# this run's budget (`aip runah --budget-tokens`). `act` waits on the child by its run file, never
# longer than the script cap allows: a child that is still going comes back as `running`, and
# the next pass waits again.
#
# It ships inside the package as a bundle (src/aip/server/bundles/assist.rl, compiled from this
# folder), as build_procedure does.

Procedure assist
  "Do a task with the catalog's procedures: run the one that fits, build one when none does, answer what the runs ask, and ask the person when stuck."

  Use_When
    "A task is to be done with the procedures in the catalog, or with one built for it, run ahead by runah."
    "Run it with `aip runah assist -i '{\"task\": \"...\", \"outcome\": \"\"}'`; on a continuation, outcome is the person's answer."
  Do_Not_Use_When
    "The procedure to run is already known: run it with `aip runah` directly."
  Requires python 3.10
  Avoid
    "Changing the catalog: retiring, pinning, or publishing over a name that exists."
    "Finishing with an answer the outcomes of the runs do not support."

Start "The task; outcome is empty at first, the person's answer on a continuation." {
  task: string    "What is to be done, in the requester's words."
  outcome: string "Empty to begin; when the person is answering a question this run asked before, their answer."
  Next_Step search
}

Execute search "List the catalog's procedures that may fit the task, with what each takes." {
  Read task
  Run_Script scripts/search.py
  Produce catalog: string "The procedures that may fit, best first: name, what it does, when to use it, its inputs."
  Next_Step work
}

Loop work Until done, At_Most 50, Else_Exit {
  Task_Agent plan "One model call: which procedure to run next, with what inputs, or done." {
    Read task, outcome, catalog
    Prompt assets/plan.md
    Produce run:    string        "A procedure name, a folder, or the run id of a run to carry on; empty when done."
            inputs: string        "Its inputs as a JSON object; for a run id, {\"answers\": ...} or {} to wait."
            note:   string        "The answer to the task, or the question for the person, when done; empty otherwise."
            done:   true_or_false "Whether the task is done or the person must be asked."
    Next_Step act
  }

  Execute act "Run it through the aip client: start the run, or carry one on, and wait on it within the script cap." {
    Read run, inputs
    Run_Script scripts/runah.py
    Produce outcome: string "What the run came to, as JSON: status, run_id, and the result, the pause or the error."
    Continue
  }

  Next_Step end
}

End "The answer, or the question for the person." {
  Read note
}
